Description: Performs the general Bayesian estimation method of
    linear-bilinear models for genotype x environment interaction of
    Perez-Elizalde, Jarquin and Crossa (2012) <doi:10.1007/s13253-011-0063-9>:
    the additive main effects and multiplicative interaction (AMMI) model
    and the sites regression (SREG, GGE) model, with the data of an earlier
    trial as the prior (conjugate normal and von Mises-Fisher priors weighted
    by its replicates) or with vague priors; a compiled Gibbs sampler;
    posterior summaries with highest posterior density intervals;
    convergence diagnostics; biplots with highest posterior density regions;
    DIC and WAIC; a plain-language interpretation of every result; and a
    built-in 'shiny' application. For
    Bayesian stability analysis in general (regression and variance models,
    stability indices, probabilities of superior performance), see the
    package 'bayesstability'.
